cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software and the paper."
type: software

title: "capp-gpt-cmca-encoder: Cross-Modal Contrastive Alignment of B-Rep Graphs with Manufacturing Feature Prototypes"

abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of the CMCA Part Encoder for CAPP-GPT. Encodes a
  CAD boundary representation as a face graph: per-face UV grids through a CNN,
  per-face and per-edge attributes, and a Graph Transformer whose attention bias
  compares attribute similarity, real shared-edge face adjacency, their sum, and
  a shuffled-adjacency control. Faces are classified by cosine similarity to
  learned manufacturing-feature prototypes under a prototype InfoNCE objective,
  rather than by a fixed classification head. Extending the label tower while
  leaving the geometry tower unchanged is an architectural affordance; unseen
  classes are not evaluated. The repository contains the STEP-to-features
  extractors, the encoder, every paper experiment configuration, the saved data
  splits, and the scripts that regenerate the reported tables.

